-restricting-some-uses-of-us-and-foreign-cbdcs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a bill in Florida}}}\uc2  prohibiting federal CBDCs and foreign CBDCs, citing concerns about power shifts.\par \par \uc2 While opponents fear privacy threats, others see CBDCs as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/what-is-a-cbdc-why-central-banks-want-to-get-into-digital-currencies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blockchain adoption tool}}}\uc2 . The \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  currently has no immediate plans for a digital dollar, but the landscape may change post-2024 elections.\par \par \uc2 CBDC projects surged globally, with 100+ countries researching and 39+ nations implementing pilots, proof-of-concepts, or related initiatives, as per {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/state-of-cbdc-report-by-cointelegraph-research"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph's CBDC database}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ron-desantis-vows-to-ban-cdbc-in-the-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Continue reading\u8230\'20\'26}}}\par \par \uc2 #2 Breaking: Judge rules XRP is not a security in SEC's case against \uc2 Ripple\par \par \uc2 On July 13th, the United States District Court in the Southern District of New York granted a partial victory to \uc2 Ripple Labs\uc2  in the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 's (SEC) case dating back to 2020.\par \par \uc2 Judge Analisa Torres ruled that ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) is not a security when traded on \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchanges but is a security when sold to institutional investors. Initially, the SEC fought to restrict \uc2 Ripple\uc2 's token offering due to its alleged unregistered security status.\par \par \uc2 The case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/xrp-price-faces-a-rocky-road-to-recovery-ahead-of-sec-s-ripple-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ongoing since December 2020}}}\uc2 , witnessed a surge in the price of ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) from $0.45 to $0.61 within minutes of the news. At the time of writing, the ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) price is $0.63.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ripple-wins-case-against-sec-as-judge-rules-xrp-is-not-a-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Continue reading\u8230\'20\'26}}}\par \par \uc2 #3 More than 186 US banks well-positioned for collapse, \uc2 SVB\uc2  analysis reveals\par \par \uc2 An analysis by economists, sparked by the coll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/svb-financial-group-files-for-chapter-11-bankruptcy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apse of Silicon Valley Bank (SVB)}}}\uc2  on March 10, highlighted the vulnerability of nearly 190 U.S. banks to potential runs. Factors such as rising interest rates, a substantial share of uninsured deposits, and losses in long-term assets were revealed as threats to the banks\u8217\'20\'19 stability.\par \par \uc2 The study suggests that if only half of uninsured depositors decide to withdraw, around 190 banks could face potential risks, with up to $300 billion in insured deposits at stake.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/more-186-us-banks-well-positioned-for-collapse-svb-analysis-reveals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Continue reading\u8230\'20\'26}}}\par \par \uc2 #4 SEC lawsuits: 68 cryptocurrencies are now seen as securities by the SEC\par \par \uc2 As a result of its numerous lawsuits, the SEC expanded its classification of cryptocurrencies as securities to include at least 68 digital assets.\par \par \uc2 Combined, the lawsuits {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-s-binance-suit-contains-heady-mix-of-predictable-charges-novel-revelations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brought against Binance}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-coinbase-crypto-exchange"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coinbase}}}\uc2  introduced 23 cryptocurrencies to the SEC's list, totaling over $100 billion in market value. Notable additions include ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ), Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ), and Decentraland ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/decentraland-mana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MANA}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 SEC Chair \uc2 Gary Gensler\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-lawyers-flame-gensler-over-claims-that-all-crypto-are-securities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 commented that "everything other than Bitcoin"}}}\uc2  falls under the agency\u8217\'20\'19s remit. This legal scrutiny covers approximately 10% of the total crypto market capitalization, indicating the SEC's increasing involvement in regulating the crypto space.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-labels-61-cryptocurrencies-securities-after-binance-suit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Continue Reading\u8230\'20\'26}}}\par \par \uc2 #5 Former \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  CTO makes $2M bet on Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s performance\par \par \uc2 Former \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  CTO Balaji Srinivasan placed a $2 million bet on Bitcoin's ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) performance, and predicted it would reach $1 million within 90 days due to hyperinflation in the United States.\par \par \uc2 The wager was initiated on March 17, with Srinivasan accepting the bet against pseudonymous \uc2 Twitter\uc2  user James Medlock. The terms involve a 40:1 odds scenario, with Medlock risking $1 million worth of USD Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/usdc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDC}}}\uc2  ) and 1 ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) if Bitcoin falls short of $1 million by June 17. Bitcoin did not reach the anticipated price point within that time frame.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/former-coinbase-cto-makes-2m-bet-on-bitcoin-s-performance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Continue Reading\u8230\'20\'26}}}\par \par \uc2 #6 \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s spot \uc2 Bitcoin ETF\uc2  now listed on Nasdaq trade clearing firm \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  analyst\par \par \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 's proposed iShares spot Bitcoin exchange-traded fund (ETF) was listed on the \uc2 Depository Trust & Clearing Corporation\uc2  (DTCC), which suggests the potential for approval by the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC).\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg ETF analyst \uc2 Eric Balchunas\uc2  commented that such a listing could be part of the process before launching a crypto ETF, viewing it positively for SEC approval. The SEC has until Jan. 10, 2024, to decide on \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 's application. If approved, it may open the door for other spot crypto ETFs.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/blackrock-spot-bitcoin-etf-nasdaq-clearing-firm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Continue Reading\u8230\'20\'26}}}\par \par \uc2 #7 Here\u8217\'20\'19s how ChatGPT-4 spends $100 in crypto trading\par \par \uc2 Cointelegraph conducted a crypto-trading experiment with \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s GPT-4 version of its artificial intelligence (AI) ChatGPT, in which it allocated $100 to various cryptocurrencies based on its learned insights.\par \par \uc2 The AI recommended distributing the funds as follows: $50 to ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ), $25 to ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), $15 to Cosmos ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/cosmos-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM}}}\uc2  ), and $10 to "NFT and Web3-related projects." For its heavy position in ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ), it cited Bitcoin's \u8220\'20\'1Csafe-haven\u8221\'20\'1D status amid financial instability and potential trajectory toward $100,000.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/here-s-how-chatgpt-4-spends-100-in-crypto-trading"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Continue Reading\u8230\'20\'26}}}\par \par \uc2 #8 \uc2 Genesis\uc2  is planning to file for bankruptcy: Report\par \par \uc2 On Jan. 18 reports surfaced that Genesis Global Capital, a cryptocurrency lending firm and subsidiary of \uc2 Digital Currency Group\uc2 , was preparing to file for bankruptcy due to liquidity issues.\par \par \uc2 The bankruptcy filing followed the \uc2 U.S. SEC\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s charges against \uc2 Genesis\uc2  and crypto exchange \uc2 Gemini\uc2  for offering unregistered securities through the Gemini \u8220\'20\'1CEarn\u8221\'20\'1D program. \uc2 Gemini\uc2  co-founder \uc2 Cameron Winklevoss\uc2  claimed that \uc2 Genesis\uc2  owed the exchange $900 million.\par \par \uc2 Genesis\uc2  faced liquidity challenges linked to the collapse of Three Arrows Capital and the bankruptcy of \uc2 FTX\uc2 , where \uc2 Genesis\uc2  held approximately $175 million.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/genesis-is-planning-to-file-for-bankruptcy-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Continue Reading\u8230\'20\'26}}}\par \par \uc2 #9 Mark Cuban loses $870K in hot wallet hack\par \par \uc2 In September, the billionaire investor Mark Cuban reportedly lost nearly $900,000 in crypto from one of his hot wallets.\par \par \uc2 Blockchain sleuths spotted the hack, with assets like USD Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/usdc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDC}}}\uc2  ), Tether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tether-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDT}}}\uc2  ), and Lido Staked Ether (stETH) being withdrawn in a 10-minute window. Cuban then confirmed the hack but stated he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t sure how it happened.\par \par \uc2 This was not the first time Cuban has suffered losses in the crypto market, having {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/mark-cuban-calls-for-stablecoin-regulation-in-wake-of-iron-finance-bank-run"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suffered from a \u8220\'20\'1Crug pull"}}}\uc2  in June 2021.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/mark-cuban-hot-wallet-hacked"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Continue Reading\u8230\'20\'26}}}\par \par \uc2 #10 Missing \u8216\'20\'18Bitcoin Millionaire\u8217\'20\'19 and ONFO coin co-creator found dead: Report\par \par \uc2 Dr. \uc2 John Forsyth\uc2 , co-founder of the ONFO coin crypto project, was found dead with an apparent gunshot wound about a week after he was reported missing.\par \par \uc2 Forsyth, an emergency room doctor and crypto advocate, went missing on May 21, which led his family to raise concerns. On May 30, his body was discovered less than a mile away from the hospital where he worked. Forsyth co-founded ONFO coin in 2020, a referral-based crypto project, with his brother Richard.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-millionaire-onfo-coin-creator-dead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Continue Reading\u8230\'20\'26}}}\par \par \uc2 Magazine: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/defis-billion-dollar-secret-the-insiders-responsible-for-hacks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeFi\u8217\'20\'19s billion-dollar secret: The insiders responsible for hacks}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjMtMTIvYjFlMGJmZTktYzM2MS00ODAzLWIwMmEtYTgwZGFkNzQzZjZhLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020231226ejcq0005n\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 BTC price up 160% in 2023 \u8212\'20\'14 5 things to know in Bitcoin this week\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By William Suberg \par \uc2 1,790 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 December 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin heads toward the 2023 yearly close after a BTC price bull market comeback with barely any retracements.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) begins the Christmas holidays with a bump as BTC\u8217\'20\'19s price tests support at a crucial time.\par \par \uc2 The last week of 2023 is already seeing \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 and in the year where BTC/USD is up more than 160%, anything can happen.\par \par \uc2 What are traders\u8217\'20\'19 expectations for the yearly close?\par \par \uc2 The Bitcoin chart checkpoint is fast approaching, with price action in a range between $40,000 and current 19-month highs at $44,730.\par \par \uc2 Looking back at the events of the past 12 months, there is much to be proud of for Bitcoin bulls \u8212\'20\'14 huge network growth, repeat all-time highs for mining difficulty and hash rate, as well as an accompanying transformation in miner profitability.\par \par \uc2 On-chain metrics have also flipped into \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  territory en masse, signaling the chance that the new bull market is still in its early innings.\par \par \uc2 On the horizon are major events for all Bitcoin and crypto investors \u8212\'20\'14 a decision on the United States\u8217\'20\'19 first spot price exchange-traded fund (ETF) and the next block subsidy halving.\par \par \uc2 At this pivotal point in Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s history, Cointelegraph takes a look at the current state of the market and highlights some key topics to focus on in the countdown to the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 BTC price dices with crux $43,000 level at Christmas\par \par \uc2 After days of sideways trading, BTC price action finally offered fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the weekly close.\par \par \uc2 A dip to $42,700 on \uc2 Bitstamp\uc2  was the result, data from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://subscription.cointelegraph.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph Markets Pro}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSD/?exchange=BINANCE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\uc2  shows, before a modest recovery above the $43,000 mark.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-12/354ce915-4ac0-4d1c-b678-5aa745a31526.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 1-hour chart. Source: \uc2 TradingView\par \par \uc2 This all played into the roadmap for popular trader and analyst Credible Crypto, who over the weekend forecast a return to that area before Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-primed-to-gain-says-trader-bitcoin-eyes-45k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 next leg higher}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBids filled, all metrics look fantastic still, send it,\u8221\'20\'1D part of his latest commentary on X (formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 ) stated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAbsolutely primed for the next leg up- hopefully we get one more quick swipe into low 43k's to fill a few more of my bids first.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bids filled, all metrics look fantastic still, send it. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BTC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qs5UITMXNY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/qs5UITMXNY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CrediBULL Crypto (@CredibleCrypto) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CredibleCrypto/status/1739051477849805221?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Fellow trader Crypto Ed, creator of trading team CryptoTA, agreed that current levels needed to offer a reversal.\par \par \uc2 Santa started to offload his bags.....\par \par \uc2 If BTC should be \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , this is where it should bounce.\par \par \uc2 If no strong bounce, we go sub 40k in coming days.\par \par \uc2 Merry Xmas! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/13A60qM0YZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/13A60qM0YZ}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WL7XwoVhdL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WL7XwoVhdL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ed_NL (@Crypto_Ed_NL) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Crypto_Ed_NL/status/1739049478768709961?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 $43,000 is a divisive level; other popular commentators, notably trader Crypto Chase, see it as the point at which bulls are destined to run out of steam in the longer term.\par \par \uc2 Crypto Chase {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/early-bull-market-bitcoin-price-1st-ever-weekly-golden-cross"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added to shorts at $43,000}}}\uc2  earlier in December, continuing that the upcoming \b \highlight22\uc2 ETF approval\b0 \highlight\uc2  should mark the local top before \u8220\'20\'1Creality\u8221\'20\'1D kicks in.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BTC}}}\uc2  plan\par \par \uc2 1. 3rd drive to close shorts/play a bounce\par \par \uc2 2. TP the bounce\par \par \uc2 3. chop ensues as holiday approaches but market holds because of pending \b \highlight22\uc2 ETF approval\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 4. \b \highlight22\uc2 ETF approval\b0 \highlight\uc2  pump, re-open shorts around here\par \par \uc2 5. liquidity / reality\par \par \uc2 *not drawn to time scale\par \par \uc2 *approval price may vary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qHpG8FmmeS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qHpG8FmmeS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Crypto Chase (@Crypto_Chase) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Crypto_Chase/status/1734332674146275632?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-traders-48k-btc-price-before-etf-sell-the-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph reported}}}\uc2 , the idea that approval day will form a \u8220\'20\'1Csell the news\u8221\'20\'1D event has long been gathering popularity, including among professional trading firms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor this reason, we expect topside resistance for BTC in the 45-48.5k region and a possible retracement to 36k levels before the uptrend resumes,\u8221\'20\'1D QCP Capital wrote in its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.qcp.capital/featured-article/market-update-21-dec-23/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest market update}}}\uc2  last week.\par \par \uc2 2023: Bitcoin bounces back in classic style\par \par \uc2 Looking back at 2023, however, there is no doubt over how far Bitcoin has come.\par \par \uc2 Since the yearly open, BTC/USD has gained in excess of 160%, with 60% gains in Q4 alone, per data from statistics resource {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.coinglass.com/today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CoinGlass}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-12/66cca87d-5656-4f89-b23f-0958d761eaad.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD returns (screenshot). Source: CoinGlass\par \par \uc2 Even this month has produced 15% gains so far \u8212\'20\'14 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s best December since 2020 \u8212\'20\'14 despite not repeating the breakout beyond all-time highs seen at the time.\par \par \uc2 Coming after its longest-ever bear market, this renaissance has been music to the ears of long-term holders, who, as Cointelegraph reported, have stubbornly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-hodl-waves-2020-bull-market-buyers-supply"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to sell BTC}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This behavior has endured despite the \u8220\'20\'1Cup-only\u8221\'20\'1D nature of the year\u8217\'20\'19s price performance, with upside tempered by only modest consolidations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of the standout features of the 2023 market has been the remarkably shallow depth of all price pullbacks and corrections,\u8221\'20\'1D on-chain analytics firm Glassnode wrote in the latest edition of its weekly newsletter, \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://insights.glassnode.com/the-week-onchain-week-51-2023/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Week On-Chain}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D on Dec. 19.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHistorically, periods of bear market recovery, and bull market uptrends for BTC regularly see at least -25% pullbacks from the local high, with many examples exceeding -50%. However, the deepest correction in 2023 closed just -20% below the local high, suggesting that buy-side support, and the overall supply and demand balance has been favourable all year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-12/798e8bb7-5fb0-47eb-92be-fb4b753117d0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin bull market corrections annotated chart (screenshot). Source: Glassnode\par \par \uc2 That \u8220\'20\'1Cfavorable\u8221\'20\'1D climate has led all Bitcoin investor cohorts back to aggregate profitability, yet as Glassnode notes, this is not so high as to spark mass selling and risk an uptrend breakdown.\par \par \uc2 Examining the Net Unrealized Profit/Loss (NUPL) metric, researchers showed that profitability currently echoes mid-2019, when Bitcoin saw a mid-cycle high.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe NUPL metric for each cohort is not yet at euphoric highs, but is also comfortably above the respective cohort break-even level,\u8221\'20\'1D they summarized.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-12/2fdf3010-8dc5-4bea-aaca-a37b5e652367.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin NUPL annotated chart (screenshot). Source: Glassnode\par \par \uc2 At $43,000, meanwhile, BTC/USD remains 37% below its current all-time high.\par \par \uc2 Macro markets wrap up a year of rate hikes\par \par \uc2 In a typically quiet holiday week, there is little expected when it comes to macroeconomic \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  catalysts for risk assets.\par \par \uc2 U.S. markets are not trading for much of the remainder of 2023, with jobless claims the last data print of interest for the year, due on Dec. 28.\par \par \uc2 Key Events This Week:\par \par \uc2 1. Markets Closed, Merry Christmas! - Monday\par \par \uc2 2. Initial Jobless Claims - Thursday\par \par \uc2 3. Pending Home Sales data - Thursday\par \par \uc2 4. Crude Oil Inventory data - Thursday\par \par \uc2 The markets are wrapping up a busy 2023 with a quiet week.\par \par \uc2 Happy Holidays everyone!\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Kobeissi Letter (@KobeissiLetter) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KobeissiLetter/status/1738936158346694966?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 This leaves markets cautiously optimistic for major macro policy changes to come next year. Months of U.S. data have fed the narrative of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-shirks-us-pce-inflation-win-bitcoin-buyers-42k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declining inflation}}}\uc2  with barely any exceptions.\par \par \uc2 Now, the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  faces the question of when to begin unwinding interest rate hikes \u8212\'20\'14 a move known as a \u8220\'20\'1Cpivot\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 and how fast.\par \par \uc2 As Cointelegraph reported, bets on the move\u8217\'20\'19s timing include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-whale-games-warning-btc-price-40k-us-data"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as early as next month}}}\uc2 , while the Fed itself has played down such odds.\par \par \uc2 Per data from \uc2 CME Group\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cmegroup.com/markets/interest-rates/cme-fedwatch-tool.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FedWatch Tool}}}\uc2 , markets remain unconvinced that officials will lower rates at the next meeting of the Federal Open Market Committee, or FOMC, on Jan. 31.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-12/b29e204e-981d-4033-84c3-aacc786425ba.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Fed target rate probabilities chart. Source: \uc2 CME Group\par \par \uc2 How good do Bitcoin miners really have it?\par \par \uc2 When it comes to Bitcoin success stories of 2023, nothing arguably tops network fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 Both hash rate and difficulty have offered a rags-to-riches transformation this year, and the trend shows no sign of stopping with the next halving just months away.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-12/13c911f3-fd97-4655-9325-19a194e9e32e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin network fundamentals overview (screenshot). Source: BTC.com\par \par \uc2 According to data from monitoring resource {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://btc.com/stats/diff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC.com}}}\uc2 , mining difficulty is due to hit yet more all-time highs at its next adjustment, this not due until early January. The latest adjustment saw nearly 7% added \u8212\'20\'14 the fourth-highest uptick of 2023, taking difficulty to 72 trillion.\par \par \uc2 The same is true of hash rate, as miners deploy ever more processing power amid a surge in profitability.\par \par \uc2 Revenue collected via transaction fees by bitcoin miners averaged nearly $2,000,000 per day in 2023. This is up 400% year over year. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zZjUwy1Gbh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zZjUwy1Gbh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jameson Lopp (@lopp) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lopp/status/1738547873967435907?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The presence of Ordinals inscriptions has boosted fee revenue considerably in the second half of the year \u8212\'20\'14 in mid-December, the proportion of their income from fees hit 37%, per Glassnode {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://studio.glassnode.com/metrics?a=BTC&m=mining.RevenueFromFees"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-12/c52d3042-114e-4a95-bbc9-39ed99ba06df.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin % miner revenue from fees chart. Source: Glassnode\par \par \uc2 Some commentators argue that miners are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-46k-2024-halving-interview-filbfilb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeking to hoard BTC}}}\uc2  into the halving, which will immediately cut the reward per block by 50%.\par \par \uc2 For Glassnode lead on-chain analyst Checkmate, however, there is a sobering lesson amid the apparent miner comeback.\par \par \uc2 The golden era for accumulating BTC was years ago, he lamented last week, revealing that he bought in at the exact top of the 2017 bull market.\par \par \uc2 My claim to fame is I bought the exact top of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Bitcoin?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Bitcoin}}}\uc2  in 2017. My buy was so bad, that the extra \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  fee applied for AUD at the time put my bid above the top tick of the top candle.\par \par \uc2 My pain hardly compares to that of miners.\par \par \uc2 Since 2017, mining Difficulty is up 4,130%, and\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vN5edmMXuf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vN5edmMXuf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 _Check\u625\'02\'71ate \u9889\'26\'A1\u9762\'26\'22\u65039\'FE\'0F\u65039\'FE\'0F (@_Checkmatey_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/_Checkmatey_/status/1738510913769177161?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Greedy for gains this Christmas\par \par \uc2 Despite the slower pace of BTC price gains toward the end of the year, the average investor is increasingly guided by a sense of greed.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/price-analysis-12-22-btc-eth-sol-bnb-xrp-ada-avax-doge-dot-link"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 12/22: BTC, ETH, SOL, BNB, XRP, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, DOGE, DOT, LINK}}}\par \par \uc2 This is the final conclusion of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://alternative.me/crypto/fear-and-greed-index/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto Fear & Greed Index}}}\uc2 , the popular sentiment gauge that looks set to round out 2023 at levels seen during Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s $69,000 all-time high two years ago.\par \par \uc2 At 73/100 as of Dec. 25, the Index, which uses a basket of factors to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/explained/what-is-the-crypto-fear-and-greed-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compute the average mindset}}}\uc2  across the crypto investor base, is firmly in its \u8220\'20\'1Cgreed\u8221\'20\'1D bracket.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-12/61d96004-af2a-4b14-9e65-e4efed50ecff.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto Fear & Greed Index (screenshot). Source: Alternative.me\par \par \uc2 As Cointelegraph reported, sustainability of the bull market as viewed through the lens of Fear & Greed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/inherently-bearish-below-41-5-k-5-things-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should not pose a problem}}}\uc2  just yet. Throughout past price cycles, only readings above 90/100 have market macro market turnarounds.\par \par \uc2 With November 2021 being a conspicuous exception, the question for hodlers now is a classic one: Is this time different?\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjMtMTIvZDAyZDVjNTQtYTAxYi00NjVlLTg4ODktODM0NzRhZGUzYjBmLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020231226ejcp0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Buy bitcoin\par \b \uc2 How to buy Bitcoin in India\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Dilip Kumar Patairya \par \uc2 1,561 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 December 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Various options to buy Bitcoin in India include centralized and decentralized crypto exchanges, SIPs and P2P exchanges.\par \par \uc2 The grand old cryptocurrency has had plenty of aficionados in the Indian crypto space. Consensus and \uc2 YouGov\uc2  conducted a global survey on crypto and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/what-is-web-3-0-a-beginners-guide-to-the-decentralized-internet-of-the-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Web3}}}\uc2  in unison. They published a report on June 23, revealing that 32% of Indians had bought cryptocurrencies at some point, and 21% still owned digital assets. It also revealed that Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) dominated the cryptocurrencies purchased.\par \par \uc2 Levying a 30% tax on income received from digital assets didn\u8217\'20\'19t dent the sentiment in the country regarding cryptocurrencies. According to a report published by the \uc2 KuCoin\uc2  cryptocurrency exchange, the digital assets market in India is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kucoin.com/blog/kucoin-into-the-cryptoverse-india-report-reveals-optimistic-prospects-for-market-growth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected}}}\uc2  to clock $241 million by 2030.\par \par \uc2 As the world\u8217\'20\'19s most populous country, with 1.4 billion people, India comes across as a country with millions of prospective cryptocurrency investors. Based on data from the \uc2 United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific\uc2 , 68% of this demographic falls within the 15\u8211\'20\'1364 age range, indicating a higher likelihood of interest in cryptocurrencies such as BTC.\par \par \uc2 This article explains how to buy Bitcoin in India on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/centralized-vs-decentralized-crypto-exchanges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 centralized and decentralized exchanges}}}\uc2 , systematic investment plan (SIP), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/explained/crypto-otc-trading-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over-the-counter (OTC) deals}}}\uc2  or direct {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/what-is-p2p-trading-and-how-does-it-work-in-peer-to-peer-crypto-exchanges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 peer-to-peer (P2P) exchanges}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 How to buy BTC on a centralized crypto exchange in India\par \par \uc2 Catering to millions of prospective Bitcoin buyers, there are hundreds of centralized exchanges operating in India, both local and multinational. One needs to check factors such as ease of use, security and low fees when zeroing in on an exchange.\par \par \uc2 One needs to complete the exchange registration process, including verifying their phone number and email. The next step is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/what-is-kyc-and-why-do-crypto-exchanges-require-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Know Your Customer (KYC)}}}\uc2 , a government-mandated procedure that requires the person to submit a soft copy of their identification documents with the exchange. A team verifies these documents before giving access to the applicant. KYC regulations aim to prevent financial crimes such as identity theft and money laundering.\par \par \uc2 One can buy Bitcoin via OTC or P2P trading on a centralized exchange. OTC trading has a minimum order size. For instance, CoinDCX has a minimum order size of 15,000 Tether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tether-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDT}}}\uc2  ) or 12,00,000 Indian rupees (whichever is lesser), while WazirX OTC Desk serves large crypto volumes worth $50,000 and above.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-12/e7965aef-9780-4eed-bd41-8615405b2377.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 One may take the P2P route to buy BTC for lower denominations. The role of the exchange is to facilitate a direct deal between the buyer and the seller while acting as an escrow, ensuring nobody is at a loss. The exchange holds the money paid to the seller. Once the buyer receives BTC, the amount is transferred. The buyer can pay in fiat or any other cryptocurrency acceptable to the seller.\par \par \uc2 How to buy BTC on a decentralized crypto exchange in India\par \par \uc2 As the name suggests, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/what-are-decentralized-exchanges-and-how-do-dexs-work"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decentralized exchange (DEX)}}}\uc2  is designed to facilitate P2P transactions without any decisive role for a single person or a group of executives. Instead, based on the input provided by participants, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/what-are-smart-contracts-a-beginners-guide-to-automated-agreements"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 smart contract executes the transactions}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Direct transactions between users on the blockchain eliminate any need for DEXs to act as intermediaries. As trades get executed on top of the blockchain network via a smart contract, every transaction incurs a fee along with the trading fee. This is, however, less than what one incurs on centralized exchanges. Unlike centralized exchanges, DEXs do not take custody of users\u8217\'20\'19 funds, so the end-user always controls their digital assets.\par \par \uc2 To execute a transaction on a DEX, one needs to connect their cryptocurrency wallet to the exchange. However, DEXs don\u8217\'20\'19t allow buying Bitcoin with fiat currency, so one needs to transfer another cryptocurrency for Bitcoin. Transactions can be conducted without fulfilling KYC requirements. While transactions on DEXs might be anonymous for now, they could be brought into the regulatory ecosystem as it evolves.\par \par \uc2 How to buy Bitcoin via SIP in India\par \par \uc2 A systematic investment plan is a disciplined approach to regularly invest a fixed amount in assets at predefined intervals. SIP allows one to keep buying Bitcoin consistently over a predefined period. SIPs have been a fundamental component of conventional market instruments, including stocks and mutual funds. Thanks to SIPs, investors can capitalize on market fluctuations while retaining their portfolios for a long time.\par \par \uc2 To invest in SIPs, one needs to download the app of a service provider offering SIPs, complete the registration and KYC procedures, and select the relevant option on the screen. The next step is to choose the coin one wants to invest in (in this case, BTC), set the day and frequency of the plan, and start the SIP.\par \par \uc2 How to make direct P2P crypto transactions in India\par \par \uc2 To conduct direct peer-to-peer crypto transactions, one can opt for either on-exchange or off-exchange methods. On-exchange transactions involve using a P2P service on a crypto exchange platform where users register, complete identity verification (KYC), and then browse and initiate transactions with other users. The platform holds the cryptocurrency in escrow until both parties confirm the transaction.\par \par \uc2 Off-exchange or OTC transactions require finding a trusted buyer or seller, often through personal networks or OTC brokers, and directly agreeing on transaction terms. Payment is usually made via bank transfer or digital wallets, and the cryptocurrency is transferred directly to the receiver\u8217\'20\'19s wallet. In both methods, it\u8217\'20\'19s important to prioritize security and adhere to local regulations.\par \par \uc2 Direct P2P cryptocurrency transactions can be conducted through several popular P2P Bitcoin exchanges, such as Paxful, OKX, WazirX and Hodlhodl.com. These platforms facilitate the buying and selling of Bitcoin and other cryptocurrencies directly between individuals, offering various payment options, including bank transfers and online wallets.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-12/8c7a8dbf-4a28-4c18-a6c3-a818c7640daa.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-12/cd6e0bc9-a894-47bd-80b6-cd681da6b6bb.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 They typically charge low trading fees, provide noncustodial wallets, and use escrow services to enhance security. With features like auto-matching and multiple payment methods, these exchanges cater to diverse needs while ensuring user safety and minimizing the risk of fraud and hacks in the P2P crypto market.\par \par \uc2 Modes of payment for cryptocurrency transactions in India\par \par \uc2 Crypto exchanges in India allow one to transfer money using bank transfer (debit card or credit card) via Immediate Payment Service (IMPS) and \uc2 Unified Payments Interface (UPI)\uc2 . When conducting P2P trading, the seller might take payments in any mode they prefer, along with regular IMPS and UPI. These modes include regular Paytm, a digital payment service, and Lightning UPI, fast real-time transactions on Paytm with a single click without a PIN.\par \par \uc2 One can also pay for BTC using other cryptocurrencies, such as Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s DOT ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) and Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), though many sellers prefer using stablecoins, such as USDT and USD Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/usdc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDC}}}\uc2  ). However, buying Bitcoin via \uc2 PayPal\uc2  is not supported in India yet.\par \par \uc2 Methods to store Bitcoin\par \par \uc2 After buying Bitcoin, the next step is to store it securely. One can choose from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/bitcoin-wallets-a-beginners-guide-to-storing-btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 several types of Bitcoin wallets}}}\uc2 , such as desktop wallets, mobile wallets, online wallets, hardware wallets and paper wallets. Many buyers leave their Bitcoin with the exchange, which may not be suitable because the exchange holds the cryptocurrency and not the buyer.\par \par \uc2 Hardware wallets and paper wallets store Bitcoin offline, making it safe from thieves, though one still has to be careful not to lose the private key or the paper wallet itself. Mobile wallets have the advantage of convenience, and one can carry their BTC around and use it the way they want at any time. Desktop and online wallets typically offer a level of security comparable to keeping Bitcoin on an exchange.\par \par \uc2 Wallets can also be categorized as custodial or noncustodial. When storing funds in custodial wallets, users have no {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/how-to-backup-your-crypto-wallet-private-keys"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 control over their private keys}}}\uc2 , and funds lie in the custody of a third party. In contrast, noncustodial wallets give users complete control over their private keys and, subsequently, their funds.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-12/b041d6ac-cf98-4b17-a7d8-e2b131a79237.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin regulations in India\par \par \uc2 Indian law requires anyone who has made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/cryptocurrency-regulations-in-india"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gains from trading virtual digital assets (VDAs),}}}\uc2  including Bitcoin, to pay tax at a rate of 30% plus 4% cess, a tax levied on the tax for spending on a specific purpose. When buying Bitcoin on an Indian exchange, the onus to ensure compliance is on the exchange.\par \par \uc2 However, when buying BTC on an international exchange or conducting a P2P transaction where BTC exchanges hands, the buyer and seller must ascertain that compliance requirements are met.\par \par \uc2 Should you buy Bitcoin in India?\par \par \uc2 Although purchasing Bitcoin in India presents possible investment prospects, careful thought must be given. Regulatory uncertainties exist despite the legality of cryptocurrencies. Decision-making is impacted by variables such as market \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a lack of detailed guidelines and prospective policy changes.\par \par \uc2 Accessibility via exchanges that facilitate rupee transfers is a benefit; however, there are still restrictions on some payment options. It\u8217\'20\'19s critical to assess one\u8217\'20\'19s own risk tolerance, comprehend market dynamics, and stay current on regulatory changes.\par \par \uc2 Even though Bitcoin offers opportunities for investing, careful consideration and knowledge of India\u8217\'20\'19s changing cryptocurrency scene are necessary before making any decisions.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjMtMTIvNDcwZGM0NzQtODEyNS00ZjczLTgxYmYtOWU3OWYxMDFjZDRhLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020231226ejcp0000c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
