ays"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 altcoins have outperformed Bitcoin}}}\uc2  over the same period. \uc2 AVAX\uc2  has particularly competed fiercely with BTC, almost tripling over the last three months. \uc2 SOL\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  have rallied 267% and 150% respectively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-12/a272b228-9ac7-4e17-9e54-4bb03e871f58.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and Altcoin\u8217\'20\'19s three-month performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/4jBlMmW7/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 On the shorter timeframe, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-is-cardano-price-down-today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano}}}\uc2  is leading the gains among the largest cryptocurrencies by market capitalization after rising 12% over the last 24 hours. The other top layer 1 token \uc2 Solana\uc2  comes in second with 10% on the gains on the day, while Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s DOT has increased by 9.2% over the same period.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, despite reclaiming the key $42,000 level, Bitcoin posted only 3% gains on Dec. 13, suggesting that it is still trailing the altcoins. But can we really speak about the start of another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/is-it-altseason-altcoin-30-day-performance-and-total-market-cap-flash-bullish"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 altcoin season}}}\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/price-analysis-12-13-btc-eth-bnb-xrp-sol-ada-doge-avax-dot-matic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 12/13: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP, SOL, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , DOGE, AVAX, DOT, MATIC}}}\par \par \uc2 Has altcoin season arrived?\par \par \uc2 Crypto trader Remen wrote in an X (formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 ) post that he believes the recent dump could push altcoins into another bull run. He added that it would take a long period of chops for the big crypto to resume an uptrend, as BTC dominance has topped out.\par \par \uc2 I told you about flash dumps repeatedly\par \par \uc2 Now dump is completed\par \par \uc2 It will take a long period of chops for Bitcoin to resume uptrend\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin dominance topped\par \par \uc2 We now entering proper ALT SEASON\par \par \uc2 BE POSITIONED\par \par \uc2 Tears of regret don\u8217\'20\'19t taste great\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 RamenPanda (@IamRamenPanda) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IamRamenPanda/status/1734038730623877461?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Even though some signs are there, it may still be too early to confirm the altcoin season. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/what-is-an-altcoin-a-beginners-guide-to-cryptocurrencies-beyond-bitcoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Altcoins}}}\uc2  are digital assets other than Bitcoin and the crypto community recognizes an altcoin season when the majority (at least 75%) of the top 50 coins by market cap outperform Bitcoin for 90 days. This has only been seen for a few altcoins, and it remains to be seen if more will follow suit.\par \par \uc2 According to Data from Blockchain Center, only 53% of the top altcoins have outperformed BTC during the last three-month period. Although this is a positive sign, it is still not enough to declare an altcoin season.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-12/933f132c-758c-42c3-92c0-ef20fa69121c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Altcoin season index. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.blockchaincenter.net/en/altcoin-season-index/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Blockchain Center}}}\par \par \uc2 In addition, Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s market cap dominance is still above 50% since crossing this level on Oct. 1, reaching a high of 55.26% on Oct. 6, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-dominance-hits-54-ahead-btc-halving"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highest in over two and a half years}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-12/c11176b5-cc04-45f9-8068-f228e317a77d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC market cap dominance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/QroWXOMD/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-dominance-likely-top-btc-price-eyeing-45k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin dominance}}}\uc2  fell to 52% on Dec.11 and as the price continued to dump, the crypto community began chanting the start of \u8220\'20\'1Caltcoin season.\u8221\'20\'1D At the time of writing, BTC dominance is back to around 53.06%, just above its 50-day exponential {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/3-ways-traders-use-moving-averages-to-read-market-momentum"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moving average}}}\uc2  (EMA).\par \par \uc2 However, it remains to be seen if the oldest crypto will hold its position or if altcoins will continue rallying, with the shorter-term view showing that crypto markets could remain range-bound.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjMtMTIvMWU0YTZiMzUtYmEzZi00YmY3LWI2ZWYtNDIxODQzNDA1MDZlLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020231214ejce000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
